,"r":"dish/tanindon","n":"Tanindon","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Oyakodon, literally \"parent-and-child donburi\", is a donburi, or Japanese rice bowl dish, in which chicken, egg, sliced scallion (or sometimes regular onions), and other ingredients are all simmered together in a kind of soup that is made with soy sauce and stock, and then served on top of a large bowl of rice. The name of the dish is a poetic reflection of both chicken and egg being used in the dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tanindon"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanindon"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Benihana","dish/benihana"],["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Bincho","dish/bincho"],["Boxer Ramen","dish/boxer-ramen"],["Cagen","dish/cagen"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Em (restaurant)","dish/em-restaurant"],["Esaki (restaurant)","dish/esaki-restaurant"],["Feng Sushi","dish/feng-sushi"],["Freshness Burger","dish/freshness-burger"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Heihachi Jaya","dish/heihachi-jaya"],["Hitsumabushi","dis